WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:05.920
There are people in my audience and elsewhere
who are getting too confident about the upcoming

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:06.990
presidential election.

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:08.440
I'm scared by it.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:10.030
You guys are scaring me.

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:14.580
And so what I want to do today is to make
the case that not only could Donald Trump

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:20.130
win reelection, nothing major really needs
to change for him to win reelection.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:24.110
He could be winning right now from an Electoral
College standpoint.

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:31.220
So if you don't look at the details and you
say, oh, Biden's plus 10, Biden's plus twelve,

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:33.460
there was a poll where Biden was plus fifteen.

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:38.050
Seems like Biden's winning easily and he's
also winning key battleground states.

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:42.260
Biden is going to run away with a historic
Electoral College victory.

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:44.310
No, no.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:50.400
If by the end of this clip, I have not convinced
you that we should be very careful of interpreting

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.220
the data we have in that way.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:54.030
Then I will have failed to do my job.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:56.490
I deserve to be canceled.

00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:57.670
Hello.

00:00:57.670 --> 00:01:01.850
If by the end of this segment, I've not convinced
you that we need to be very, very careful

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:03.280
about what's going on.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:05.880
So let's start with national polling.

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:09.580
Whenever there there's a poll that says Joe
Biden is up 12.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:11.100
Joe Biden is up 10.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:12.470
Joe Biden is up 15.

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:13.590
It gets a ton of attention.

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:19.810
And certainly if Joe Biden wins the popular
vote by 10 to 12 or 15, Trump's done.

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:24.729
That's not actually what the mathematical
case today is.

00:01:24.729 --> 00:01:28.520
Let's look at the numbers today and understand
the numbers.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:33.450
First of all, the polls that had Biden up
ten, twelve and fifteen, we're not getting

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:34.790
any more of those polls.

00:01:34.790 --> 00:01:35.790
OK.

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:39.630
The last poll where Biden was up double digits
was July 20, 30 was up 10.

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:40.729
More recently.

00:01:40.729 --> 00:01:44.020
Biden is only up three in a number of polls.

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:48.210
And on average, Biden is up by six point four.

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:50.520
Six point four is very different than 15.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:51.520
My friends.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:55.450
So six point four still sounds pretty good.

00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:59.689
But understand that if you look at any individual
poll, you have to understand the margin of

00:01:59.689 --> 00:02:00.689
error.

00:02:00.689 --> 00:02:01.689
Hugely important.

00:02:01.689 --> 00:02:08.989
So, for example, the latest YouGov poll has
a three point three percent margin of error.

00:02:08.989 --> 00:02:16.950
So when the YouGov poll says that Biden is
winning by nine 49 to 40, Trump's 40 could

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:18.980
actually be forty three point three.

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:22.329
And it would still be within the margin of
error of the poll.

00:02:22.329 --> 00:02:26.859
Biden's forty nine could really be forty five
point seven.

00:02:26.859 --> 00:02:34.900
So a poll which promotes as a headline Biden
plus nine could really be Biden plus.

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:36.440
Two point four.

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:39.129
And the poll would still be correct.

00:02:39.129 --> 00:02:40.540
This is what we.

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:44.989
This is why we have a confidence interval
and a margin of error.

00:02:44.989 --> 00:02:51.239
If Biden is really only winning by two point
four, Trump could win the Electoral College.

00:02:51.239 --> 00:02:56.810
Remember, we have polling for the national
popular vote, but we have an electoral college

00:02:56.810 --> 00:02:58.840
system in 2016.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:04.120
Hillary won the popular vote by I think it
was two point one or two point two, but lost

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:05.230
the Electoral College.

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:11.919
So for people who are saying what could happen
to allow Trump to catch up to Biden, nothing

00:03:11.919 --> 00:03:16.029
has to happen within the margin of error to
day.

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:21.010
Donald Trump has the support where he could
win the Electoral College.

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:27.010
If we have similar battleground results to
those in 2016, you don't need an October surprise

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:29.309
when the current lead for Trump might only
be.

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:32.629
I'm sorry, the current lead for Biden might
only be two point four.

00:03:32.629 --> 00:03:37.239
Trump won 2016 with a two point one percent
deficit in the popular vote.

00:03:37.239 --> 00:03:40.549
So that's national popular vote polling.

00:03:40.549 --> 00:03:42.449
Let's now go to step two.

00:03:42.449 --> 00:03:47.209
You might say Biden is winning hugely in key
battleground states.

00:03:47.209 --> 00:03:54.279
Well, remember, in 2016, the national popular
vote polls were accurate, but there were state

00:03:54.279 --> 00:03:57.729
polls that didn't get it right.

00:03:57.729 --> 00:04:00.810
State polls had some problems in 2016.

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:04.089
So Hillary was winning the polling in Wisconsin.

00:04:04.089 --> 00:04:07.010
Going into the election, Trump won Wisconsin.

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:08.729
That's just one example.

00:04:08.729 --> 00:04:13.979
So once you concede the national polling,
that looks like a big lead for Biden could

00:04:13.979 --> 00:04:17.209
actually be like a two point lead for Biden.

00:04:17.209 --> 00:04:21.950
State polling was off in some states in 2016.

00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:26.010
You have to come to the conclusion that Biden
might not really be winning electorally right

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:27.010
now.

00:04:27.010 --> 00:04:29.560
And then lastly, I talked about this yesterday.

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:34.600
When you look at voter registration, it doesn't
look that great.

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:39.560
It is true that in many states, if you look
only at new registrations, meaning people

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:43.950
who have never been registered before, who
maybe were not even 18 years old in 2016,

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:48.250
when you look just at new registrations, Democrats
have an advantage over Republicans.

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:50.310
They've registered more new voters.

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:57.730
But as I told you yesterday in Florida, Pennsylvania,
Arizona, Iowa and North Carolina, in terms

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:05.030
of the number of registered Democrats versus
Republicans today versus 2016, the advantage

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:09.160
has been in favor of Republicans and against
Democrats.

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:14.160
And the reasons for this are people who have
moved from one state to another.

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:17.670
People who have switched party registrations,
deaths.

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:21.190
This is separate from who is going to choose
to vote.

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:23.440
But this is not the type of data you want
to see.

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:26.560
If you want to be confident that Joe Biden
is going to run away with this thing.

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:33.850
So when you step back and you say, well, the
polls, if you account for margin of error,

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:36.110
look very similar to 2016.

00:05:36.110 --> 00:05:40.700
There were state polls in 2016 that were wrong.

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:45.050
And then you realize, you know, over the next
three months, if the economy improves a little

00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:46.170
bit.

00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:53.120
If Corona virus, it gets better if we get
a vaccine or a good treatment, that Trump

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:59.460
will try to take credit for a one or one and
a half point swing from where we are today

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:01.020
in Trump's direction.

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:03.130
And Trump wins the Electoral College.

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:10.400
So I hope that I have convinced you that we
need to be far more skeptical about these

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:14.200
Bidens running away with it, ideas that we
are starting to see.

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:17.500
You must run as if we are behind.

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:19.920
This is going to be a huge fight.

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:24.110
It actually doesn't look nearly as good as
some are claiming.

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:30.130
And I'm very worried some of you are worrying
me that we are getting complacent, that some

00:06:30.130 --> 00:06:36.000
people think the data clearly points to Biden
running away with this review, this video.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:41.230
If you need to fact check me, go item by item.

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:47.300
And if you do, you can come to only one conclusion,
which is that there is not actually evidence

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:51.050
to say right now that Joe Biden is going to
easily win in November.

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:54.100
He might win hugely and he might lose.

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:55.770
And we've got to we're going to have to fight
this.

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:58.880
We're going to have more coverage of this
on the show's Instagram page.

